{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence","id":438246,"title":"Eating for Essence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-12T04:04:46-07:00","id":438246,"title":"Eating for Essence","content":"So... Uratha can do Aggravated damage if they eat someone... Is this because they add some supernatural soul-reaving effect, or is it there to represent the massive chunks of flesh torn away? Because if it is the latter... there is literally no downside to it, because then the Werewolf just has to tear off the flesh, and then spit it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T04:22:30-07:00","id":438267,"title":"","content":"I think that's supposed to be <i>really hard to do. </i>Like, you get it in your mouth and you can just taste all the essency goodness and some part of you starts chanting <i>SWALLOW SWALLOW SWALLOW...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T04:22:53-07:00","id":438269,"title":"","content":"I believe it's like first edition, where you have to bite with the intent to eat for essence. It's a mix of both massive damage from eating someone's body and the spirit part of you that channels Father Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:13:39-07:00","id":438311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438267#post438267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's supposed to be <i>really hard to do. </i>Like, you get it in your mouth and you can just taste all the essency goodness and some part of you starts chanting <i>SWALLOW SWALLOW SWALLOW...</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... but shouldn't that be represented somehow? I mean... there is no indication of it when one does a simple bite attack.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I like this. It's a way, way too easy method of dealing Aggravated damage to things. Sure, it's a breaking point, but so is using Silver (albeit in the other direction), and it's only marginally worse than killing Uratha (That one is -2, this one is -3)... If you go out to kill that Pure pack that's been terrorizing the area, you have no reason NOT to use eat-attacks in combat. It removes the big benefit from Gauru, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:36:09-07:00","id":438324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438311#post438311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah... but shouldn't that be represented somehow? I mean... there is no indication of it when one does a simple bite attack.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I like this. It's a way, way too easy method of dealing Aggravated damage to things. Sure, it's a breaking point, but so is using Silver (albeit in the other direction), and it's only marginally worse than killing Uratha (That one is -2, this one is -3)... If you go out to kill that Pure pack that's been terrorizing the area, you have no reason NOT to use eat-attacks in combat. It removes the big benefit from Gauru, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe the reason to not use it is that while your character does not like the pure, <i>eating members of your own species alive</i> is a tad extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:39:33-07:00","id":438328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438324#post438324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe the reason to not use it is that while your character does not like the pure, <i>eating members of your own species alive</i> is a tad extreme.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but let's not forget that Uratha are very inhuman in their mindsets. There is a pretty large part that is Spirit, and to a spirit, there is nothing more natural than eating your own for sustenance (Hence the severe penalty on the breaking point check).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:56:09-07:00","id":438345,"title":"","content":"It's a matter of not looking at it from a <i>mechanical</i> point of view but rather a <i>playable</i> one. If you do that, every NPC your ST runs pretty much has carte blanche to cast you out, or worse, just for starters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:58:13-07:00","id":438349,"title":"","content":"Only if you get caught doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:02:28-07:00","id":438354,"title":"","content":"Sense direction of your missing werewolf friend's blood points you directly into another werewolf's belly.<br /> <br /> While ideally packmates will respect each others' privacy, they have a lot of information gathering abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:08:32-07:00","id":438359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438345#post438345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a matter of not looking at it from a <i>mechanical</i> point of view but rather a <i>playable</i> one. If you do that, every NPC your ST runs pretty much has carte blanche to cast you out, or worse, just for starters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the problem here is that I am the ST, and I'm trying to find a reason for Fire-Touched and Predator Kings not to use this as their main way of fighting Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:13:56-07:00","id":438364,"title":"","content":"It's still a horrible thing to do from their perspective, too, is the thing.Fire-Touched have no reason to <i>want</i> to eat the flesh of infidels. The Inquisition didn't run around eating people; they burned them at the stake. The Predator Kings might use such a tactic but it's still intrinsically <i>anathema</i> to them. That said, it's a good way to make them dangerous.<br /> <br /> If you're the ST, you can find other ways to have the Pure fight. You're not limited to the most practical but least justifiable practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:14:00-07:00","id":438365,"title":"","content":"The Fire Touched have at least some incentive to leave Forsaken alive so they can convert them. <br /> <br /> Predator Kings... Yeah, I got nothing this is exactly the shit they'd pull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:18:32-07:00","id":438367,"title":"","content":"Plus it's always a breaking point, they might not want to reach 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:20:51-07:00","id":438369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438364#post438364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still a horrible thing to do from their perspective, too, is the thing.Fire-Touched have no reason to <i>want</i> to eat the flesh of infidels. The Inquisition didn't run around eating people; they burned them at the stake. The Predator Kings might use such a tactic but it's still intrinsically <i>anathema</i> to them. That said, it's a good way to make them dangerous.<br /> <br /> If you're the ST, you can find other ways to have the Pure fight. You're not limited to the most practical but least justifiable practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It was anathema, back when the scale was a &quot;that way lies disaster&quot;-scale. Now it just points towards more spirit-like behaviour. And the Fire Touched are <i>very</i> spirit-friendly, if their 2e write-up is any indication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438365#post438365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fire Touched have at least some incentive to leave Forsaken alive so they can convert them.<br /> <br /> Predator Kings... Yeah, I got nothing this is exactly the shit they'd pull.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. But when it comes to bloody battle, when the time has come to show whose ideology is the strongest, et cetera.. Then this is the ultimate tool.<br /> Yes, gifts like Savage Rending and Silver Jaws are gone.. but they aren't needed. Every single Werewolf now has the ability to deal Aggravated damage at will. And I don't like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:48:24-07:00","id":438383,"title":"","content":"The best way to fight a werewolf is like a crocodile. You need to jump on their back and try to clamp their mouth shut, because the jaws are the most dangerous bit by far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:48:28-07:00","id":438384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438359#post438359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the problem here is that I am the ST, and I'm trying to find a reason for Fire-Touched and Predator Kings not to use this as their main way of fighting Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they also swear they won't commit cannibalism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T09:12:56-07:00","id":438509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438384#post438384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they also swear they won't commit cannibalism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, where it is? I remeber the Oath of Wolf to have &quot;Pure do not kill Pure&quot;, but I did not recall the cannibalism thing.<br /> <br /> Also, what if Pure goes in to Death Rage and eat some Uratha then - does is the violation of Oath and Breaking Point? Or it is &quot;pass&quot;, as character was not doing sane descisions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T09:27:23-07:00","id":438551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438369#post438369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. It was anathema, back when the scale was a &quot;that way lies disaster&quot;-scale. Now it just points towards more spirit-like behaviour. And the Fire Touched are <i>very</i> spirit-friendly, if their 2e write-up is any indication.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah. But when it comes to bloody battle, when the time has come to show whose ideology is the strongest, et cetera.. Then this is the ultimate tool.<br /> Yes, gifts like Savage Rending and Silver Jaws are gone.. but they aren't needed. Every single Werewolf now has the ability to deal Aggravated damage at will. And I don't like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with earlier posters in that while I agree mechanically this is true I'm just not seeing it easily done in a narrative sense. As the ST you've got a whole plethora of reasons why only the occasional werewolf or group would commit this practice. For the Forsaken its a blatant violation of the Oath, which is kind of that set of cultural customs they feel defines their identity. Sure there will be specific circumstances where you have to break it, as with all codes (just killing another werewolf is one, so they're already in violation when trying to kill Pure and they know it). By consuming the flesh of another wolf for any reason they're committing an extreme taboo (for most) on either side. Even the Pure have a vested interest in keeping with Harmony (and their own version of the Oath which I feel probably covers this). Harmony breaks aren't just a mechanical slap on the wrist for these guys. Breaking towards spirit enough means they or their packmates are sliding towards not &quot;more spirit-like behavior&quot; but towards becoming an actual spirit monster trapped in the Hisil with multiple bans, unable to control your own rage and flying towards it at breakneck speed. No matter who you are, Forsaken or Pure, I think this is seen as a serious problem.<br /> <br /> Those issues aside I'm also having a hard time imagining where this is the more convenient damage option for any werewolf. Sure this might be the case if two packs went toe-to-toe with each other using no tactics or other advantages, but if Forsaken and Pure are hunting each other they know it and are acting accordingly, this means pulling in every favor you've got from the nearby human population and Spirit Wilds, choosing a battlefield you prefer if you can, pack silver (if Forsaken), target others instead of the Werewolves themselves. In most engagements werewolves will have enough options that deciding to start consuming your enemy won't be too high on the list.<br /> <br /> While the Forsaken will start packing silver, and one could apply the same argument I did above to its use, it is a lesser breaking point that's easier to deal with, and is also seen by werewolves at large as more a hopefully rare necessary evil. Saying &quot;Ah, screw it&quot; when the chips are down and eating your enemies which also happens to be as addicting as a drug and against your very nature as a descendant of Father Wolf (this I feel would be a major reason why the Pure would frown on the practice, if it goes against their perceived image of Father Wolf they'll repress it sternly, even violently) is rather extreme to me. It is true that I haven't seen it explicitly stated cannibalism is rejected amongst the Pure in 2e, I'd say there's plenty of evidence that its very likely. Though you are the ST, so you could make them have regular barbeque's if you really wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-12-2015, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:02:23-07:00","id":438692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438509#post438509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, where it is? I remeber the Oath of Wolf to have &quot;Pure do not kill Pure&quot;, but I did not recall the cannibalism thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I forget which number it is but I think it's 'Do not eat the flesh of Human or wolf.'<br /> <br /> Part of the thing to remember is even in first edition it was acceptable to lose Harmony. I know I've spoken to a lot of people who viewed loss of Harmony or Humanity or whatever the 'morality' stat was on their games as 'Game Over' but it was never really like that. You didn't want to go all the way down to 0 and you didn't want to lose it all the time, but a breaking point then or now represent a change to your character based on their actions. Due to their hybrid nature, werewolves are really affected by it now, but it's not that bad either way. Even a 10 or 0 Harmony werewolf can theoretically work their way back to balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:11:01-07:00","id":438696,"title":"","content":"it seems better now then it was before. Before, when you became a broken soul you were usually put down like a rabid dog. There was a lodge dedicated to bringing you back but it was damn near impossible for some without any willpower. Now adays ya just gotta walk into mcdonalds and eat yourself some wholesome gmo filled crap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:36:58-07:00","id":438729,"title":"","content":"This is complicated only slightly by the lack of McDonalds in the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":