rsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438759#post438759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh right forgot about those. What about in cases where the spiritual touchstone is wilderness itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you get rid of a ghost that's anchored to a stretch of road or a body of water?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438763#post438763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where exactly are you getting a McChicken when you can't leave the <i>Hisil</i>? I'm pretty sure even a spirit of trans fat doesn't count as processed food.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bVisitors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T18:38:38-07:00","id":439188,"title":"","content":"Exactly, have the pack bring it in. But then again if you have a pack that gives a damn you won't fall that far. The only example I could think of would be a bale hound, and they usually give themselves up unintentionally before it gets that bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T18:46:00-07:00","id":439196,"title":"","content":"Since Harmony has moved away from being a morality track Bale Hounds probably wouldn't fall into that trap. Particularly since so many of the vices they attempt to propagate are so based in the Flesh.<br /> <br /> Defiling loci, using silver weapons, bringing spirits into the world, mating with humans, they're all breaking points towards the Flash.<br /> <br /> That's, of course, providing a straight conversion of existing Bale Hounds to 2e rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-12-2015, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T18:53:45-07:00","id":439216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=439196#post439196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Harmony has moved away from being a morality track Bale Hounds probably wouldn't fall into that trap. Particularly since so many of the vices they attempt to propagate are so based in the Flesh.<br /> <br /> Defiling loci, using silver weapons, bringing spirits into the world, mating with humans, they're all breaking points towards the <b>Flash</b>.<br /> <br /> That's, of course, providing a straight conversion of existing Bale Hounds to 2e rules.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cyIIYerdlUA\" data-code=\"cyIIYerdlUA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/cyIIYerdlUA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T18:59:26-07:00","id":439224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=439216#post439216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cyIIYerdlUA\" data-code=\"cyIIYerdlUA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/cyIIYerdlUA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That is the correct response, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T19:01:37-07:00","id":439225,"title":"","content":"What can I say Speed Force and Kicking Space-Conqueror Ass are just the natural evolution of being a Bale Hound. Pure at heart doesn't necessarily mean pure good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:06:58-07:00","id":439479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=438551#post438551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree with earlier posters in that while I agree mechanically this is true I'm just not seeing it easily done in a narrative sense. As the ST you've got a whole plethora of reasons why only the occasional werewolf or group would commit this practice. For the Forsaken its a blatant violation of the Oath, which is kind of that set of cultural customs they feel defines their identity. Sure there will be specific circumstances where you have to break it, as with all codes (just killing another werewolf is one, so they're already in violation when trying to kill Pure and they know it). By consuming the flesh of another wolf for any reason they're committing an extreme taboo (for most) on either side. Even the Pure have a vested interest in keeping with Harmony (and their own version of the Oath which I feel probably covers this). Harmony breaks aren't just a mechanical slap on the wrist for these guys. Breaking towards spirit enough means they or their packmates are sliding towards not &quot;more spirit-like behavior&quot; but towards becoming an actual spirit monster trapped in the Hisil with multiple bans, unable to control your own rage and flying towards it at breakneck speed. No matter who you are, Forsaken or Pure, I think this is seen as a serious problem.<br /> <br /> Those issues aside I'm also having a hard time imagining where this is the more convenient damage option for any werewolf. Sure this might be the case if two packs went toe-to-toe with each other using no tactics or other advantages, but if Forsaken and Pure are hunting each other they know it and are acting accordingly, this means pulling in every favor you've got from the nearby human population and Spirit Wilds, choosing a battlefield you prefer if you can, pack silver (if Forsaken), target others instead of the Werewolves themselves. In most engagements werewolves will have enough options that deciding to start consuming your enemy won't be too high on the list.<br /> <br /> While the Forsaken will start packing silver, and one could apply the same argument I did above to its use, it is a lesser breaking point that's easier to deal with, and is also seen by werewolves at large as more a hopefully rare necessary evil. Saying &quot;Ah, screw it&quot; when the chips are down and eating your enemies which also happens to be as addicting as a drug and against your very nature as a descendant of Father Wolf (this I feel would be a major reason why the Pure would frown on the practice, if it goes against their perceived image of Father Wolf they'll repress it sternly, even violently) is rather extreme to me. It is true that I haven't seen it explicitly stated cannibalism is rejected amongst the Pure in 2e, I'd say there's plenty of evidence that its very likely. Though you are the ST, so you could make them have regular barbeque's if you really wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valid points all, but I'll point out that Killing Werewolves is a severe breaking point towards Flesh (-2), and eating Werewolf flesh is a breaking point both towards Flesh (-2, Breaking the Oath) and Spirit (-3, eating).<br /> <br /> I suppose the worst act is the one that should be rolled for, but if one does two severe flesh-breaks with one action, and one somewhat worse one towards Spirit... how should I force the roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:34:51-07:00","id":439560,"title":"","content":"I think the book says it's always towards spirit. I guess since eating your own kind is a really spirity thing to do the method trumps it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:42:02-07:00","id":442865,"title":"","content":"I missed something about this thread guys.<br /> <br /> The book clearly say:<br /> <i>''When devouring flesh <u><b>for Essence</b></u>, the Uratha causes aggravated wounds.''</i><br /> <br /> I find this very tricky.<br /> So, If I eat the damn shoulder of a vampire, I don't eat it for essence, obviously. But I still cause aggravated damage?<br /> This question can sound stupid I know, but the book is very clear. ''Devouring flesh for Essence''.<br /> <br /> (mage are awakened humans so... I think an uratha can eat flesh <i>for essence </i>from a mage.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:15:30-07:00","id":442928,"title":"","content":"I think you'd still get essence from a vampire, and definitely a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:18:13-07:00","id":442933,"title":"","content":"I have some doubts about the vampires. They're dead after all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:24:26-07:00","id":442940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, If I eat the damn shoulder of a vampire, I don't eat it for essence, obviously. But I still cause aggravated damage? </div> </div> </div>No. You cannot try to weasel your way to Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This question can sound stupid I know, but the book is very clear. ''Devouring flesh for Essence''.<br /> <br /> (mage are awakened humans so... I think an uratha can eat flesh <i>for essence </i>from a mage.) </div> </div> </div>It can from a human (including mages), is muddy as if it is possible at all from a kindred. Note that if you attack to get essence you swallow the chunk of flesh, wich in the case of vampires may count towards the vinculum and Vitae adiction. It's also a Breaking point towards Spirit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:55:18-07:00","id":443005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=442940#post442940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. You cannot try to weasel your way to Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It can from a human (including mages), is muddy as if it is possible at all from a kindred. Note that if you attack to get essence you swallow the chunk of flesh, wich in the case of vampires may count towards the vinculum and Vitae adiction. It's also a Breaking point towards Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I totally agree with everything you said.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T13:21:13-07:00","id":443021,"title":"","content":"Here's where my curiosity sparks. I remember reading about vampires feeding on other supernatural creatures and the side effects they gain from their vitae. Will those same effects apply to werewolves when they feed from other supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T13:30:52-07:00","id":443045,"title":"","content":"I don't believe them being dead has any bearing on it. That's why we've had lodges of cannibalism and the Eaters of the Dead lodge.<br /> <br /> @Cecoyotl<br /> In first edition if you eat a changeling the Essence you get has a Resonance, tainted with madness. Eating a fetch provides no Essence, as they revert to their component parts. Prometheans require twice as much flesh to get any Essence from them, and eating their flesh inflicts Disquiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T13:33:52-07:00","id":443050,"title":"","content":"The Bone Gnaw facet mentions that if the bone in question is more than 6 months old it's &quot;lost it's flavour&quot; but if it's less than that then it still counts as a harmony violation. If you were feeling charitable you could say that <i>young</i> vampires provide essence, but any that have been dead for more than half a year don't. Just an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T14:04:29-07:00","id":443082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence?p=439196#post439196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defiling loci, using silver weapons, bringing spirits into the world, mating with humans, they're all breaking points towards the Flash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I just found this typo ridiculously amusing.<br /> <br /> edit. To keep this somewhat on topic, at the moment I wouldn't count vampires as Human for the purposes of eating them for Essence. I could see that being a Lodge granted ability or something the Bale Hounds could get as part of a Gift, Merit or equivalent ability.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 03-15-2015, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join D